---
description: >-
  The markdownAlwaysOn twin of label-syntax.mmd: the same special
  sequences with the setting on, so every special is markdown. The plain
  **bold** _ital_ special draws bold and italic, the bare backticks and the
  code span draw inline code; tags, \n and the quoted markdown string draw
  as in the default picture, which this one differs from. The terminals
  stay as written in both (D710).
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
railroad-ebnf-beta
plain = "**t**" , ? special **bold** _ital_ ? ;
quoted = "`t`" , ? "`special **bold** _ital_`" ? ;
bare = "<b>t</b>" , ? `special **bold** _ital_` ? ;
code = "t" , ? special a `code` b ? ;
tags = "t" , ? special <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O ? ;
newline = "t" , ? special one\ntwo ? ;
